+Set `COOP_SANITIZE=1` to build with AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer:
+
+```bash
+COOP_SANITIZE=1 ./tests/coop/build_and_run.sh
+```
+
+## Protocol overview
+
+Each datagram uses a fixed 20-byte header with:
+
+- magic `TFCP`;
+- protocol version;
+- packet type and flags;
+- session ID;
+- sequence number;
+- payload length.
+
+Multi-byte fields are serialized explicitly in network byte order. Player snapshots are sequenced and sent unreliably. Gameplay actions that must not disappear use event IDs, ACKs, retransmission, and duplicate suppression.
+
+The handshake compares a 32-bit FNV-1a compatibility hash derived from the TFE build identifier, co-op protocol version, and sampled content from the core Dark Forces GOB archives.
+
+## Source layout
+
+```text
+TheForceEngine/TFE_DarkForces/Coop/
+  coop.cpp             Dark Forces integration and remote ghost
+  coop.h               engine-facing API
+  coopProtocol.*       wire protocol and serialization
+  coopSession.*        handshake, state transfer, reliability, timeout
+  coopTransport.*      Windows/POSIX nonblocking UDP transport
+
+tests/coop/
+  coopProtocolTest.cpp
+  coopSessionTest.cpp
+  build_and_run.sh
+```
+
+## Next engineering milestones
+
+The next milestone should replace independent world simulation with a host-authoritative entity protocol:
